      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "23251473"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Although it belongs to the tubulin--tyrosine ligase family, the TTL domain lacks some of the ATP binding sites predicted to be essential for TTL activity (PubMed:23251473). Lacks tyrosine ligase activity in vitro (PubMed:23251473). Lacks glutamylation activity in vitro (By similarity). Although TTLL12 contains a potential SET-like domain in the N-terminus, it does not have lysine methyltransferase activity towards histone in vitro (PubMed:23251473)"
    }
   ],
